<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		ZK-4305 Rerender — a client-side rerender after the popup has been created
		must not abort the box's mount.

		"z-daterangebox" is already the default zclass, so setZclass() below
		rerenders the widget without changing a single class name — the rerender
		itself is what is under test, not any CSS effect of it.

		Steps to verify:
		1. Click the calendar button once, then close the popup with Cancel.
		2. Click "rerender" — no JavaScript error may appear.
		3. Click the calendar button again — the popup must open.
	</label>

	<vlayout spacing="10px" hflex="1">
		<daterangebox id="drb" format="yyyy-MM-dd" width="360px"/>
		<hlayout>
			<button id="btnRerender" label="rerender" onClick='drb.setZclass("z-daterangebox")'/>
		</hlayout>
	</vlayout>
</zk>
